-description: "Eye Of Hermes (EOH), built on God's Eye View (bilawalsidhu/gods-eye-view, MIT): the same 11 composable godseye_* tools (godseye_view, godseye_query, godseye_layers, godseye_feeds, godseye_annotate, godseye_nav, godseye_track, godseye_scene, godseye_watch, godseye_capture, godseye_admin) for public data (aircraft, ships, satellites, quakes, fires, weather, infrastructure) backed by its MCP server, a live 3D globe pane in Hermes Desktop and the Webapp that Hermes can drive and read, and HUD summaries generated with the Hermes model (ctx.llm) instead of OpenAI. An Overlays sidebar (godseye_annotate op=overlays) lists pins, routes and trails, lines, areas, watches, and scenes, and imports or exports eoh.overlays.v1 JSON under plugin-data. godseye_scene director ops build, update, list, play, and stop a Director scene on the pane; godseye_annotate op=clip stores a YouTube or X URL on a pin; godseye_feeds op=fire_check runs FIRMS, the clearest recent image, then imagery before/after, and does not create a watch or a pin. v0.2.2 hardens Wayback imagery releases, overlays when the relay is out-of-process, pane routing timeouts, and layer/user-pref behavior; v0.2.3 keeps a visible imagery surface during compare swipe and the Wayback timeline; v0.2.4 captures the pane after render and falls back to public Overpass mirrors for OSM queries; v0.2.5 restores a clean plugin.yaml and adds a strict duplicate-key test; v0.2.6 declares street-level keys through Hermes requires_env/get_secret and removes the Gods Eye View env-file fallback. v0.2.7 addresses catalog security review (public-only fetches, scoped credentials, confined imports and minimal child environments) and bounds pane captures with explicit transport errors. v0.2.8 documents the public SDR receivers layer (sdr-receivers); the map layer needs gods-eye-view main at or after b361a25 (PR #5). v0.2.9 treats watch-alert titles as quoted third-party data, requires confirm=true for godseye_admin start/stop/rest