+name: vitrail
+title: Vitrail
+repo: https://github.com/elomkdn/vitrail
+sha: "b8b4dc851a14fe2b566648beb30d7a484b6cf6f7"
+description: "Live GLSL shaders in the chat. Ask for a visual and the model writes a Shadertoy-style fragment shader that animates inside the reply in Hermes Desktop, with the sliders, colour pickers and switches it declared as annotated uniforms. Before vitrail_render returns, the Desktop half compiles the shader with WebGL 2 on the user's GPU and reports the verdict, so a compile error goes back to the model with the driver log and the model fixes it in the same turn; a still frame comes back too, for models with a vision tool. The card is drawn through a tool media renderer where Desktop has one and through a ::vitrail transcript directive where it does not (Desktop 0.22.5). Other surfaces (Telegram, CLI, TUI) get a standalone HTML player of the same shader. Adds a gallery page with hover-to-play tiles, GLSL copy and 1920x1080 PNG export, the vitrail_render and vitrail_library tools, the vitrail:shader-studio skill, and post_tool_call / transform_llm_output hooks that append the shader's delivery line (MEDIA file or directive) when a reply lacks it. Disclosure — no network calls, no shell commands, no credentials, no telemetry; GLSL written by the model runs on the user's GPU through WebGL 2 in the Desktop window; files are written only under plugin-data/vitrail (per shader: source, standalone HTML player, GPU report, a 640x360 JPEG still, exported PNGs); the still's path is given to the model, which may open it with its vision tool; while a Desktop window is open its half calls the plugin's own local route once a minute so the tool knows a GPU is listening and which transcript surface it has, and vitrail_render then waits up to 6 s for the verdict."
+maintainer: elomkdn
+tier: community
+category: desktop
+requires_hermes: ">=0.23.0"
+docs_url: https://github.com/elomkdn/vitrail#readme
+version: "0.1.0"
+image: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/elomkdn/vitrail/b8b4dc851a14fe2b566648beb30d7a484b6cf6f7/assets/banner.jpg
+screenshots:
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/elomkdn/vitrail/b8b4dc851a14fe2b566648beb30d7a484b6cf6f7/assets/desktop-chat.jpg
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/elomkdn/vitrail/b8b4dc851a14fe2b566648beb30d7a484b6cf6f7/assets/desktop-gallery.jpg
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/elomkdn/vitrail/b8b4dc851a14fe2b566648beb30d7a484b6cf6f7/assets/desktop-library.jpg
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/elomkdn/vitrail/b8b4dc851a14fe2b566648beb30d7a484b6cf6f7/assets/vitrail.jpg
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/elomkdn/vitrail/b8b4dc851a14fe2b566648beb30d7a484b6cf6f7/assets/lagoon.jpg
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/elomkdn/vitrail/b8b4dc851a14fe2b566648beb30d7a484b6cf6f7/assets/lumignon.jpg
+readme: true
+platforms: []
+known_issues:
+  - "The live card needs Hermes Desktop 0.22.5 or later with the plugin's Desktop switch on in Capabilities → Plugins (it is off by default); other surfaces get the standalone HTML player."
+  - "On a Desktop without tool media renderers the card is drawn from a ::vitrail directive; a messaging platform that shares the chat while that Desktop is open shows the directive as a line of text."
+  - "GPU verification needs a Desktop window connected to the Hermes that runs the agent; without one the shader is saved unverified and compiles when it is shown."
+  - "Shaders are single-pass and procedural: no textures, buffers or audio inputs."
+capabilities:
+  provides_tools:
+    - vitrail_render
+    - vitrail_library
+  provides_hooks:
+    - post_tool_call
+    - transform_llm_output
+  provides_middleware: []
+  requires_env: []
